  "note": "Confirm (REVEAL-5, ED-9): one atomic mutation covering reveal, update, replace and move — the server derives which, the request never says. It names the sealed version the sheet displayed (CANVAS-34), an explicit non-empty list of field keys, the audience — the table, or a list of participant ids (owner decision O-3: a group display is per-recipient copies of ONE disclosure, and a named group is expanded into its member ids by the client, so no group id and no wildcard is ever sent or stored) — and BOTH the session it was composed for and that session's reveal epoch, so a number from last night can never match tonight (ED-9). No campaign id: the session names the campaign, and ownership is the route's (SEC-3), as with CuePlayRequest.",
